What you've learned so far

At this point, you should clearly understand:

Gateway accepts external traffic.
VirtualService decides which version receives traffic.
DestinationRule maps logical subsets (blue/green) to Pod labels.
Both Blue and Green Pods run simultaneously.
Only one version receives production traffic at a time.
Traffic switching and rollback are accomplished by updating the VirtualService, not by recreating Pods or Deployments.

This mental model is essential. Once it's clear, the YAML we'll write tomorrow will feel straightforward because you'll understand why each resource exists, not just how to configure it.